Nitrous acid is used in the preparation of diazonium salts. The $-\text{N}_2^+$ group in the diazonium ion can be replaced with $Cl$, Br or CN as shown.

The reagent used is a copper(I) salt, CuX.

{{figure:pdf_visual_01.png}}

This reaction can be used in the synthesis of compound Z as shown.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}
